", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b24b5221897408360f06092324539fc71c1fbcc3f080b875c97fd09f16bebac7", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nFunctor of points.\nFor any <MATH_0001> there is a contravariant\nfunctor\n<MATH_0002>\nwhich takes an object <MATH_0003> to the set\n<MATH_0004>. In other words <MATH_0005> is a presheaf.\nGiven a morphism <MATH_0006> the corresponding map\n<MATH_0007>\ntakes <MATH_0008> to <MATH_0009>. We will always denote\nthis presheaf <MATH_0010>.\nIt is called the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>representable presheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> associated to <MATH_0011>.\nIf <MATH_0012> is the category of schemes this functor is\nsometimes referred to as the\n<EMPHOPEN_0001>functor of points<EMPHCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0013>.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6706795f223adc29c1835d0ee9fcb1e60be6d4a8dcd0c1ceb60373d44b1e65b4", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:001O:example/0001"}, "state": "READY"}, "inventory:categories:001P:lemma/0001": {"context_hash": "sha256:9c2b1c67dbe07dd8c6d2376098d8ae1c4b42e927a35b92e51c4e3ffda0f17a4b", "inventory_id": "inventory:categories:001P:lemma/0001", "kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 20318, "byte_start": 19691, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:2a5052d951cf1e928456104a391eaabfaf366e9dae4c7b7ae9205d410ed9909a", "line_end": 558, "line_start": 540}, "owner_tag": "001P", "parent_tag": "001L", "semantic_path": "lemma/0001", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "001L", "placeholders": {"ENVARGEND_0001": "]", "ENVARGOPEN_0001": "[", "LOCKED_0001": "\\label{lemma-yoneda}", "LOCKED_0002": "\\begin{reference}\nAppeared in some form in \\cite{Yoneda-homology}. Used by Grothendieck in a\ngeneralized form in \\cite{Gr-II}.\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$U, V \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$s : h_U \\to h_V$", "MATH_0003": "$\\phi : U \\to V$", "MATH_0004": "$h(\\phi) = s$", "MATH_0005": "$h$", "MATH_0006": "$F$", "MATH_0007": "$U$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})}(h_U, F) \\longrightarrow F(U),\n\\quad\ns \\longmapsto s_U(\\text{id}_U).\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{lemma}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{lemma}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:db993da333ca058eebd298f6661afc328088822e613f5bd0deb7acd3205f86f0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:59f1336290199d42199d776d0d1a2d6d51ffea52fa376b39f101fd3f61bcc6dc", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001><ENVARGOPEN_0001>Yoneda lemma<ENVARGEND_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\n<LOCKED_0002>\nLet <MATH_0001>.\nGiven any morphism of functors <MATH_0002>\nthere is a unique morphism <MATH_0003>\nsuch that <MATH_0004>. In other words the\nfunctor <MATH_0005> is fully faithful. More generally,\ngiven any contravariant functor <MATH_0006> and any object\n<MATH_0007> of <MATH_0008> we have a natural bijection\n<MATH_0009>\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:23f41fdc74b0e5d6190667a6c98e6d852b61adb61e1f8b04209fdb8e393b19bd", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:001P:lemma/0001"}, "state": "READY"}, "reference:categories-remark-big-categories": {"context_hash": "sha256:ad860c63d18f0419cf7ee665e5fe256ea043a457ee870efa83f140bd03380e99", "kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 4422, "byte_start": 2478, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:67f8624c8987b067e029d9e39dbd82ed79a8ad52a2cde1960a9e566b5c45b7fe", "line_end": 115, "line_start": 76}, "owner_tag": "0015", "parent_tag": "0013", "requested_label": "categories-remark-big-categories", "requested_tag": "0015", "semantic_path": "remark/0001", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "0013", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{remark-big-categories}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$\\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\textit{Ab}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\textit{Groups}$", "MATH_0006": "$G$", "MATH_0007": "$G\\textit{-Sets}$", "MATH_0008": "$G$", "MATH_0009": "$R$", "MATH_0010": "$\\text{Mod}_R$", "MATH_0011": "$R$", "MATH_0012": "$k$", "MATH_0013": "$k$", "MATH_0014": "$\\textit{Top}$", "MATH_0015": "$X$", "MATH_0016": "$\\textit{PSh}(X)$", "MATH_0017": "$X$", "MATH_0018": "$X$", "MATH_0019": "$\\Sh(X)$", "MATH_0020": "$X$", "MATH_0021": "$X$", "MATH_0022": "$\\textit{PAb}(X)$", "MATH_0023": "$X$", "MATH_0024": "$X$", "MATH_0025": "$\\textit{Ab}(X)$", "MATH_0026": "$X$", "MATH_0027": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0028": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0029": "$\\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0030": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0031": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0032": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0033": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{dpa-section-divided-power-rings}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{remark}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\item", "STRUCT_0009": "\\item", "STRUCT_0010": "\\item", "STRUCT_0011": "\\item", "STRUCT_0012": "\\item", "STRUCT_0013": "\\item", "STRUCT_0014": "\\item", "STRUCT_0015": "\\item", "STRUCT_0016": "\\item", "STRUCT_0017": "\\item", "STRUCT_0018": "\\item", "STRUCT_0019": "\\item", "STRUCT_0020": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0021": "\\end{remark}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:75989370749413a256a057563f7b29aba589eb9cfca025fe952ce9239d90193a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:64e50e7c7274b0d327af71b57159b0bb0e4f4ba186eb9f62f3ffa554e03438eb", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nBig categories. In some texts a category is allowed to have a proper\nclass of objects. We will allow this as well in these notes but only\nin the following list of cases (to be updated as we go along).\nIn particular, when we say: ``Let <MATH_0001> be a category''\nthen it is understood that <MATH_0002> is a set.\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> The category <MATH_0003> of sets.\n<STRUCT_0004> The category <MATH_0004> of abelian groups.\n<STRUCT_0005> The category <MATH_0005> of groups.\n<STRUCT_0006> Given a group <MATH_0006> the category <MATH_0007> of\nsets with a left <MATH_0008>-action.\n<STRUCT_0007> Given a ring <MATH_0009> the category <MATH_0010> of <MATH_0011>-modules.\n<STRUCT_0008> Given a field <MATH_0012> the category of vector spaces over <MATH_0013>.\n<STRUCT_0009> The category of rings.\n<STRUCT_0010> The category of divided power rings, see\nDivided Power Algebra, Section <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0011> The category of schemes.\n<STRUCT_0012> The category <MATH_0014> of topological spaces.\n<STRUCT_0013> Given a topological space <MATH_0015> the category\n<MATH_0016> of presheaves of sets over <MATH_0017>.\n<STRUCT_0014> Given a topological space <MATH_0018> the category\n<MATH_0019> of sheaves of sets over <MATH_0020>.\n<STRUCT_0015> Given a topological space <MATH_0021> the category\n<MATH_0022> of presheaves of abelian groups over <MATH_0023>.\n<STRUCT_0016> Given a topological space <MATH_0024> the category\n<MATH_0025> of sheaves of abelian groups over <MATH_0026>.\n<STRUCT_0017> Given a small category <MATH_0027> the category of functors\nfrom <MATH_0028> to <MATH_0029>.\n<STRUCT_0018> Given a category <MATH_0030> the category of presheaves of sets\nover <MATH_0031>.\n<STRUCT_0019> Given a site <MATH_0032> the category of sheaves\nof sets over <MATH_0033>.\n<STRUCT_0020>\nOne of the reason to enumerate these here is to try and avoid\nworking with something like the ``collection'' of ``big'' categories\nwhich would be like working with the collection of all classes\nwhich I think definitively is a meta-mathematical object.\n<STRUCT_0021>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c9f725712a0349e3d093127a6b4d8aca46e33126abe5ec409bce7f6cf30b2a29", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:0015:remark/0001"}, "state": "READY"}, "reference:categories-remark-functor-into-sets": {"context_hash": "sha256:67dfd3f8bebeb1fcce67d6bbcd429383c60b8369b13dd2f16528d245c1885a65", "kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 9487, "byte_start": 8912, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:69371291f30f874e05feedf8df575a080aea36891d47a524a500f64b381442cd", "line_end": 244, "line_start": 230}, "owner_tag": "001E", "parent_tag": "0013", "requested_label": "categories-remark-functor-into-sets", "requested_tag": "001E", "semantic_path": "remark/0001", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "0013", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{remark-functor-into-sets}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0002": "$F$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0005": "$F$", "MATH_0006": "$F(\\Ob(\\mathcal{A}))$", "MATH_0007": "$F$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0009": "$F(\\Ob(\\mathcal{A}))$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sets-section-sets-everything}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{remark}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{remark}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e64a52f350c9be9c00e58701de533b99e4ec9b13f4c17e261ba31132e6624f50", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7741349d6621714cc463329d6dd3dd11d0e22551af4f1c52b7399f23684d221b", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nSuppose that <MATH_0001> is a category.\nA functor <MATH_0002> from <MATH_0003> to <MATH_0004>\nis a mathematical object (i.e., it is a set not a class or a formula\nof set theory, see\nSets, Section <REF_0001>)\neven though the category of sets is ``big''.\nNamely, the range of <MATH_0005> on objects will be\na set <MATH_0006> and then we\nmay think of <MATH_0007> as a functor between\n<MATH_0008> and the full subcategory\nof the category of sets whose\nobjects are elements of <MATH_0009>.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7ec0248f5c19605af7025696e9e38694a10ba978f4e143c969e268e0f3a58ab4", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:001E:remark/0001"}, "state": "READY"}}, "model_output": {"hash": "sha256:b51262463b01b40e67f8cb5a3e1c13fac9153530a8270cd64d9a3c9091bd3d79", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-completion-p001-retry-raw.jsonl", "record_hash": "sha256:25d5c3e3cb39ad270c005a6e0884c388ce18e371955c287f44649a21d43baf12"}, "neighbor_unit_ids": [], "policy_revision": "git:b33b9b37f1623d49d4030a11f1661dfc29fa2ce4", "prompt_version": "translator-v2", "read_context": {"citations": [], "neighbors": [{"context_id": "inventory:categories:001O:example/0001", "relation": "before"}, {"context_id": "inventory:categories:001P:lemma/0001", "relation": "after"}], "references": [{"context_id": "reference:categories-remark-big-categories", "label": "remark-big-categories"}, {"context_id": "reference:categories-remark-functor-into-sets", "label": "remark-functor-into-sets"}], "unit_id": "tag:001L:prose-0004"}, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_required_terms": {"catalog_hash": "sha256:899a668e50f3487b37dd8781e9b5a88e3e16d272ad91b4078ac6b9d847935c12", "occurrences": [{"concept": "morphism", "projection_end": 40, "projection_start": 32, "rule": "catalog", "source_term": "morphism"}, {"concept": "natural-transformation", "projection_end": 113, "projection_start": 91, "rule": "catalog", "source_term": "natural transformation"}, {"concept": "functor", "projection_end": 125, "projection_start": 117, "rule": "catalog", "source_term": "functors"}, {"concept": "morphism", "projection_end": 176, "projection_start": 168, "rule": "catalog", "source_term": "morphism"},